  "id": "COMPOUND:14504 - PROTEIN:5011",
  "verbalization": "Metronidazole appears to interact with HCC1937 through a shared pathway involving Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside, which is a target of multiple drugs, including metronidazole. The evidence suggests that metronidazole may act as a modulator of Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside, which in turn influences HCC1937. This relationship is supported by the presence of multiple independent pathways where metronidazole targets the same intermediate, Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside, which then targets HCC1937. The consistent involvement of Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside across different targets implies a potential mechanism of action where metronidazole may regulate the activity of this compound, thereby affecting HCC1937. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside as a critical mediator in the interaction between metronidazole and HCC1937, suggesting a possible therapeutic or biological relevance.",
